-- title:
--   Local box of an adelically conjugated lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $\Lambda \subseteq D$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$. Let $\beta$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ with respect to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $x \in D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$, with $\mathbb{Q}_v$ the $v$-adic completion. Here [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda$ $v$ denotes the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the $v$-adic integers, [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ the analogous additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ an integral finite adele, [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda$ $\beta$ the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ consisting of those $d \in D$ whose image under $D \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ lies in $\beta \cdot (\text{finiteAdeleBox } \Lambda) \cdot \beta^{-1}$, and [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) $D$ $v$ the algebra map $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f} \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ obtained by tensoring the identity of $D$ with evaluation at $v$. The assertion is: $x$ lies in the local box at $v$ of `conjByFiniteIdele` $\Lambda$ $\beta$ if and only if there exists $y$ in the local box of $\Lambda$ at $v$ with $x = \beta_v \, y \, (\beta^{-1})_v$, where $\beta_v$ and $(\beta^{-1})_v$ denote the images of $\beta$ and of $\beta^{-1}$ under [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) $D$ $v$.
--
--   This identifies the $v$-adic completion of the conjugated lattice $D \cap \beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ with the conjugate $\beta_v \Lambda_v \beta_v^{-1}$ of the local box of $\Lambda$, the place-by-place description of lattice conjugation by a finite idele. It is used throughout the construction of Eichler orders and Hecke sets in the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower, where local conditions at a prime must be read off from an adelically conjugated global lattice.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_mem_localBox_conjByFiniteIdele_iff.lean

